In this example, I've used Serilog as logger implementation, but you can replace it with any other logging framework that suits your project needs. Also, the `FileUploaderFactory` is a placeholder for an assumed factory class that creates instances of the file uploader library you are using. The trade-offs between efficiency, usability, maintainability, and scalability have been considered in this implementation. For instance, the use of asynchronous operations ensures better performance when dealing with large files or varying network conditions. Furthermore, the logger provides insights into the progress and errors that may occur during file uploads.']

